---
/*
  Why you got an email from us.

  Linked from the signature of every cold email from email 2 onwards. Email 1
  carries no URLs at all.

  Copy is verbatim from docs/outreach-legal-copy.md and is deliberately plain
  rather than lawyerly, because a recipient who cannot understand it has not
  actually been informed.

  Three things this page must never grow: a booking link, a services pitch, or
  any navigation into the sales pages beyond the site's own nav. Its whole job
  is to make an annoyed stranger feel dealt with honestly, and the moment it
  tries to sell something it stops doing that job. It is also the cheapest
  protection the sending domain has: it gives a recipient somewhere to go other
  than the report-spam button.

  The exit-intent popup is suppressed here for the same reason.

  The postal address is not decorative. US anti-spam law assesses penalties per
  message, so the same address has to appear in every commercial email as well.
  If it changes here it must change in the sequences on the same day.
*/
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const email = "ernest@quademdigital.com";
const address = "18th Ahmadiyyah Avenue, Lakeside, Accra, Ghana";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Why you got an email from us | Quadem Digital"
    description="Where we got your details, why we wrote to you, and how to stop it."
    navbarScrolled={true}
    suppressExitPopup={true}
>
    <div class="outreach section-padding">
        <div class="outreach-col">
            <h1>Why you got an email from us</h1>
            <p class="standfirst">
                If you had an email from me and never asked for one, this page explains it.
                It should take a minute to read.
            </p>

            <h2>Who I am</h2>
            <p>
                I am Ernest. I run Quadem Digital, a small studio in Accra, Ghana. There is
                no sales team. The email came from me.
            </p>

            <h2>Where I got your details</h2>
            <p>
                From public sources. Your business listing, your own website, or a public
                directory. I did not buy a list and nobody passed your details on to me.
            </p>

            <h2>Why I wrote to you</h2>
            <p>
                I look at business websites and check a handful of basic things: whether the
                site loads securely, whether it works properly on a phone, whether it is set
                up so Google can describe it. When I find something worth mentioning, I write
                to the owner about that specific thing.
            </p>
            <p>
                If my email mentioned something about your website, that is where it came
                from. I looked at your site before writing.
            </p>

            <h2>What I do not do</h2>
            <p>
                I do not sell your details, share them, or add you to a newsletter. I do not
                use tracking pixels in a first email. I do not send the same message to
                thousands of people with the name swapped.
            </p>

            <h2>How to make it stop</h2>
            <p>
                Reply and say so. Anything will do. "No thanks" is enough. I will remove you
                and you will not hear from me again.
            </p>
            <p>
                You can also write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. If you would
                rather I deleted everything I hold about your business, say that and I will,
                then confirm it is done.
            </p>

            <h2>If you want to know more</h2>
            <p>
                The full detail is in the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>. You
                can ask what I hold about you, ask me to correct or delete it, or object to my
                holding it at all.
            </p>

            <div class="outreach-sign">
                <p>Ernest, Quadem Digital</p>
                <address>{address}</address>
                <p><a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .outreach {
        padding-left: 20px;
        padding-right: 20px;
    }
    /* A narrow measure, because this is a page someone reads once, carefully,
       while mildly annoyed. */
    .outreach-col {
        max-width: 660px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        font-size: 1.03rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .outreach-col h1 {
        font-family: var(--font-heading);
        font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.6vw, 2.6rem);
        line-height: 1.15;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin: 0 0 18px;
    }
    .outreach-col h2 {
        font-family: var(--font-heading);
        font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.6vw, 1.4rem);
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin: 38px 0 10px;
    }
    .outreach-col p {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        margin: 0 0 16px;
    }
    .standfirst {
        font-size: 1.12rem;
        color: var(--text-primary) !important;
    }
    .outreach-col a {
        color: var(--accent-text);
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
    .outreach-sign {
        margin-top: 48px;
        padding-top: 22px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
    }
    .outreach-sign p,
    .outreach-sign address {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        margin: 0 0 4px;
        font-style: normal;
    }
</style>
